          "path": "_m/d/j/2/4/9th-ward-of-new-orleans-wp/taken-craig-morris-dec.jpg",
          "filename": "9th Ward post-Katrina.JPG",
          "caption": "Taken by Craig Morris on Dec 22, 2006 on top of the levee overlooking the 9th Ward where the breach took place. The force of the wall of water razed all of these houses. As far as the eye can see here (roughly an area 4 blocks by 3), not a house was left standing.\nInner (southern) of the two major breaches on the east side of the en:Industrial Canal levee into the en:Lower 9th Ward; probably the one through which the en:ING 4727 came in to the neighborhood, bulldozing buildings beneath it. -- Infrogmation 02:30, 4 May 2006 (UTC)\nYes, frogman, that is where the barge came through - it was just to the right. CM, June 26, 2006",
          "alt": "Taken by Craig Morris on Dec 22, 2006 on top of the levee overlooking the 9th Ward where the breach took place. The force of the wall of water razed all of these houses. As far as the eye can see here (roughly an area 4 blocks by 3), not a house was left standing.\nInner (southern) of the two major breaches on the east side of the en:Industrial Canal levee into the en:Lower 9th Ward; probably the one through which the en:ING 4727 came in to the neighborhood, bulldozing buildings beneath it. -- Infrogmation 02:30, 4 May 2006 (UTC)\nYes, frogman, that is where the barge came through - it was just to the right. CM, June 26, 2006",
